---
layout: layouts/base.njk
description: Independent, evidence-led comparison of OSINT SaaS vendors. The first profiles are fictional examples.
---
{% import "macros.njk" as ui %}
<div class="wrap page">
  <header class="hero">
    <p class="kicker">Independent comparison</p>
    <h1>OSINT Vendor Compass</h1>
    <p class="lede">A research notebook for analysts, decision makers, and teams choosing an open-source intelligence SaaS vendor. Each profile records ownership, evidence, financial signals, customer OPSEC, sanctions exposure, and publicly named buyers.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="{{ '/compare/' | url }}">Compare vendors</a>
      <a class="button button-quiet" href="{{ '/use-cases/' | url }}">Browse by use case</a>
      <a class="button button-quiet" href="{{ '/methodology/' | url }}">How scoring works</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <dl class="stat-row">
    <div>
      <dt>Profiles</dt>
      <dd>{{ site.vendorCount }}</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Owner-approved</dt>
      <dd>{{ site.approvedCount }}</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Status</dt>
      <dd>{% if site.exampleOnly %}Example data{% else %}Mixed{% endif %}</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="read-heading">
    <h2 id="read-heading">How to read a profile</h2>
    <div class="read-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Scores, 0 to 5</h3>
        <p>Business transparency, financial health, and customer OPSEC posture. Higher means a stronger public record. OPSEC posture is about risk to the customer, not how powerful the product is.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Sanctions exposure</h3>
        <p>A risk label, not a score. Low means less recorded exposure. It covers review-list entities, ownership ties, aggregate workforce signals, and EU, UN, OFAC, and UK screening.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Known buyers</h3>
        <p>Organizations named in a public case study, contract, press release, or press report. A missing name is not proof that someone is not a customer.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="vendors-heading">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="vendors-heading">Vendor overview</h2>
      <a href="{{ '/compare/' | url }}">Open the comparison table</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      {% for vendor in vendors %}
        <article class="vendor-card">
          <p class="card-kicker">
            {% if vendor.example %}<span class="pill pill-example">Example</span>{% endif %}
            <span>{{ vendor.primary_category | categoryName }}</span>
          </p>
          <h3><a href="{{ ('/vendors/' + vendor.slug + '/') | url }}">{{ vendor.name }}</a></h3>
          <p>{{ vendor.tagline }}</p>
          <dl class="card-meta">
            <div><dt>HQ</dt><dd>{{ vendor.headquarters.city }}, {{ vendor.headquarters.country }}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Founded</dt><dd>{{ vendor.founded_year }}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Pricing</dt><dd>{{ vendor.company.pricing_model.text }}</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="score-row">
            {{ ui.scoreMeter(vendor.scores.business_transparency.score, "Transparency") }}
            {{ ui.scoreMeter(vendor.scores.financial_health.score, "Financial") }}
            {{ ui.scoreMeter(vendor.scores.customer_opsec.score, "OPSEC posture") }}
          </div>
          <div class="card-flags">
            <div>
              <p class="flag-label">Sanctions exposure</p>
              {{ ui.riskPill(vendor.jurisdiction_sanctions.risk, "sanctions") }}
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="flag-label">Known buyers</p>
              {{ ui.sectorPills(vendor.known_customers) }}
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="card-link"><a href="{{ ('/vendors/' + vendor.slug + '/') | url }}">View profile</a></p>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
